# xsched-native-async-xqueue-audit: final chain step. Packages the
# suspend/resume audit counters and destructor report that existed in
# the successful live HAL source with no published patch. No new audit
# logic: exactly the measured-source diagnostics the successful runs
# carried, so a reproduced tree pays the same per-suspend/resume counter
# overhead and prints the same XSCHED_AUDIT line at queue teardown.
#
#   preempt/include/xsched/preempt/xqueue/async_xqueue.h
#     - two relaxed atomic counters audit_suspend_count_ /
#       audit_resume_count_ next to suspended_/terminated_
#   preempt/src/xqueue/async_xqueue.cpp
#     - <cstdio>/<unistd.h> includes; destructor fprintf of the
#       XSCHED_AUDIT line (pid, xqueue handle, preempt level, suspend
#       threshold, batch size, suspend_ok, resume_ok);
#     - one fetch_add in Suspend() and one in Resume().
#
# Applies AFTER native/xsched-native-level2-source-sync.patch as chain
# step 9 (or directly on an existing eight-step prepared tree; the files
# are otherwise untouched). Origin: the live tree
# level2-build/.output/hal-native-20260908.i8na51/source, NOT the dirty
# deps working tree (the two were compared; content is identical for
# these files).
# Apply with: patch -p1 < xsched-native-async-xqueue-audit.patch
